---
layout: base.njk
title: ""
description: "Parachute is an open, self-hosted home for your notes that every AI you use — Claude, ChatGPT, your own agents — can read and write. On your machine, yours to keep and export anytime."
permalink: /
---
<style>
/* Home — single-scroll minimalist. Reuses the shared design tokens in
   style.css; only the per-screen layout lives here. */

.home {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 2rem;
}

/* Screen 1 — above the fold */
.home-hero {
    min-height: calc(100vh - 8rem);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 4rem 0 5rem;
}
.home-hero h1 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 6vw, 4.25rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1.05;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
}
.home-sub {
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.25rem;
}
.home-cta-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.25rem 1.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
}
.home-cta {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--accent);
    color: #fff;
    padding: 0.9rem 2rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    box-shadow: 0 1px 4px rgba(74, 124, 89, 0.15);
    transition: background 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
}
.home-cta:hover {
    background: var(--accent-hover);
    color: #fff;
}
.home-cta-note {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--fg-dim);
}
.home-cta-quiet {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
}
.home-trust {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
}

/* Section rhythm for screens 2–5 */
.home-screen {
    padding: 4.5rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
}
.home-eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
}

/* Screen 2 — proof image (fills the content column) */
.home-shot {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    box-shadow: 0 12px 40px rgba(44, 42, 38, 0.06);
}
/* Graceful degrade: if the PNG is missing, the alt text shows on a
   styled, aspect-reserved panel instead of a broken-image icon. */
.home-shot-frame {
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background:
        radial-gradient(120% 120% at 50% 0%, rgba(74, 124, 89, 0.05), transparent 60%),
        var(--bg-soft);
    box-shadow: 0 12px 40px rgba(44, 42, 38, 0.06);
    overflow: hidden;
}
.home-shot-frame .home-shot {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 14px;
    box-shadow: none;
}
.home-caption {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 1rem;
}

/* Screen 3 — the problem */
.home-lines {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    max-width: 38rem;
}
.home-lines li {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.6vw, 1.75rem);
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    padding: 0.85rem 0;
}
.home-lines li:last-child {
    color: var(--fg);
}

/* Screen 4 — how it works */
.home-steps {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    counter-reset: step;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.75rem;
}
.home-steps li {
    counter-increment: step;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.5rem 1fr;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    align-items: baseline;
}
.home-steps li::before {
    content: counter(step);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    line-height: 1;
}
.home-steps strong {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 500;
}
.home-steps p {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
}

/* Screen 5 — closing CTA */
.home-close {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 5rem 0 4rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
}
.home-close h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.5vw, 2.4rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
}
.home-close .home-cta {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
}
.home-close-note {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
}
.home-thin-footer {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
}
.home-thin-footer a { color: var(--fg-muted); }
.home-thin-footer a:hover { color: var(--accent); }

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .home-shot,
    .home-shot-frame {
        transition: transform 0.4s ease, box-shadow 0.4s ease;
    }
    .home-proof:hover .home-shot,
    .home-proof:hover .home-shot-frame {
        transform: translateY(-2px);
        box-shadow: 0 18px 50px rgba(44, 42, 38, 0.09);
    }
}

@media (max-width: 640px) {
    .home { padding: 0 1.25rem; }
    .home-hero { min-height: auto; padding: 2.5rem 0 3.5rem; }
    .home-screen { padding: 3.5rem 0; }
    .home-steps li { grid-template-columns: 1.75rem 1fr; gap: 0.9rem; }
}
</style>

<main class="home">
    <section class="home-hero fade-up fade-up-1">
        <h1>One memory for all your AIs.</h1>
        <p class="home-sub">An open, self-hosted home for your notes that every AI you use &mdash; Claude, ChatGPT, your own agents &mdash; can read and write. On your machine, yours to keep and export anytime.</p>
        <div class="home-cta-row">
            <a href="/install/" class="home-cta">Get started &rarr;</a>
            <span class="home-cta-note">~2 minutes, one command</span>
            <a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer" class="home-cta-quiet" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
        </div>
        <p class="home-trust">Local-first &middot; <a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io" target="_blank">Open standard (MCP)</a> &middot; Open source (AGPL)</p>
    </section>

    <section class="home-screen home-proof fade-up fade-up-2">
        <p class="home-eyebrow">See it</p>
        <div class="home-shot-frame">
            <img class="home-shot" src="/assets/home/notes-graph.png" alt="The Parachute Notes app showing notes and the links between them as a graph" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="1000">
        </div>
        <p class="home-caption">This is what you see in a few minutes &mdash; your own notes, linked.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="home-screen">
        <p class="home-eyebrow">The problem</p>
        <ul class="home-lines">
            <li>Claude, ChatGPT, Gemini &mdash; each one learns you in its own silo.</li>
            <li>Context vanishes between sessions and tools.</li>
            <li>Parachute is the one memory they all share.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="home-screen">
        <p class="home-eyebrow">How it works</p>
        <ol class="home-steps">
            <li>
                <p><strong>Install.</strong> One command brings up your hub and a browser setup wizard.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p><strong>Connect.</strong> The wizard hands you a one-paste command to point your AI at your vault.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p><strong>See it.</strong> Open Notes in your browser and watch your memory grow.</p>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="home-close">
        <h2>One memory for all your AIs.</h2>
        <a href="/install/" class="home-cta">Get started &rarr;</a>
        <p class="home-close-note">~2 minutes, one command</p>
        <nav class="home-thin-footer">
            <a href="/install/">Install</a>
            <a href="/blog/">Blog</a>
            <a href="/docs/">Docs</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
        </nav>
    </section>
</main>
